Just so that some of us won't feel entirely alone, I'll
post my own unimpressive statistics in this Nethack game.
The following numbers cover my games between September 1
and January 11, when I managed to break the logfile.lock.
Fixing the logfile is of low priority here.  At least the
the score list still works.

Best game: A Samurai whose pet killed the Quest Nemesis.
   I was carrying all sorts of useless potions and scrolls
   in my BoH, so that I could make lots of holy water and
   useful scrolls.  I cleared out the castle, and my first
   wish was for a WoC.  Unfortunately, instead of zapping
   all the stuff I amassed at my feet, I zapped myself,
   thereby unblessing my BoH.  From there on, my stupidity
   continued to drag me downhill.  I starved to death with
   34 food rations in the bag, forgetting that I could just
   drop it and loot it. (sigh)

Second Best:  Logfile says a Barbarian of mine quit on level 26
   with 84000 score.  I think that was my one Exploration test,
   where I wished for Mjollnir, cursed teleport scrolls, and
   teleport control.  I then instantly teleported to the Valley
   of the Dead.  It's easy for a low-level barbarian to get quick
   levels by killing undead with Mojo!  I noticed that that weapon
   didn't do a whole lot to energy vortices, but by that point my
   little exercise was complete.  I wasn't that interested in
   exploring anyway :)

Third Best: A Valkyrie who had cleared out the Gnomish Mines.
   The only altar she had found in the game was the one in
   the Town.  A Poly-Trap changed her briefly into a dragon,
   nuking her best armor.  She was later bitten by a wererat,
   not long after her last prayer.  In a desperate effort
   to please her god (can't use Mojo in rat form), she hoped
   to fix up the town Altar, with the help of Mojo.  The Priest
   of Tyr was not pleased....

